from the evil scientists

36
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:48,033
who shot us into space for
the invention exchange.

37
00:01:48,033 --> 00:01:51,800
But until then, we're
gonna party like it's 1990.

38
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:55,867
- [Announcer] Commercials sign
in five, four, three, two.

39
00:01:55,867 --> 00:01:57,600
Commercial sign now.

40
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,567
- We're gonna be
back in a matter

41
00:01:58,567 --> 00:02:01,067
of seconds, so stick around.

42
00:02:01,067 --> 00:02:04,167
(upbeat theme music)

43
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,267
Hey, what did you guys spike
this punch with, anyway?

44
00:02:10,267 --> 00:02:12,533
- It's 10W 30 and Tang.

45
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:14,467
- Ugh.

46
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:18,733
Act like your parents are home,
the scientists are calling.

47
00:02:18,733 --> 00:02:21,300
- Come in, Joel, my little
free floating clambake.

48
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:25,233
- Hey sir, what happened to you?

49
00:02:25,233 --> 00:02:28,433
- Well, we had a little
mishap in the lab this week.

50
00:02:28,433 --> 00:02:30,600
We were trying to make
a cold fusion Walkman,

51
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,133
and I don't know
what happened, but.

52
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:35,000
You see what happened

53
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,200
Anyway, Dr, Forrester
will be here in a second,

54
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,267
he's just trying to make
himself look presentable.

55
00:02:39,267 --> 00:02:41,967
Just make with the invention
exchange, wild boy.

56
00:02:41,967 --> 00:02:43,467
- Oh, okay, well.

57
00:02:43,467 --> 00:02:45,733
This is an invention in
honor of the party today,

58
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:47,267
that the robots are throwing.

59
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:49,700
When I was a boy, I used
to play with one of these.

60
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:53,767
All right.

61
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:57,767
And now, I'm a man, all right?

62
00:03:02,467 --> 00:03:05,000
What's your invention, sir?

63
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,367
- It's, nevermind.

64
00:03:07,367 --> 00:03:09,233
Are you okay, Clay?

65
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:10,467
- Yes, Larry.

66
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:12,533
Remember, it's all in
the name of science.

67
00:03:12,533 --> 00:03:16,900
Well, Joel, I guess our
little experiment this week

68
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:19,267
