507
00:22:34,533 --> 00:22:36,100
- [Crow] Hey that's
the same place

508
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:37,767
they filmed Robot Monster.

509
00:22:45,867 --> 00:22:47,600
- Now don't move too much.

510
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,133
I said don't move.

511
00:22:49,133 --> 00:22:51,033
We'll find out if
you're all right first.

512
00:22:51,033 --> 00:22:52,433
- [Joel] She's all
right and she'll be

513
00:22:52,433 --> 00:22:53,867
perfect for our experiments.

514
00:22:53,867 --> 00:22:56,600
- Except I could've done
this more gracefully

515
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,400
if I'd known
spectators were around.

516
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:00,267
- [Tom] Looked fine
from where I'm standing.

517
00:23:00,267 --> 00:23:01,700
- Gently now.

518
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:03,100
- No broken bones señorita?

519
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:04,300
No sharp pain?

520
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:06,067
- No really I'm all right.

521
00:23:06,067 --> 00:23:08,200
I've fallen off Lucero before.

522
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:13,200
Not for many years but I
really can ride gentlemen.

523
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,800
- Hank Scott.

524
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,800
Dr Arturo Ramos.

525
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:21,833
- Oh the luck of the Alvares.

526
00:23:21,833 --> 00:23:23,967
Come off a horse and then
right next to a doctor.

527
00:23:23,967 --> 00:23:25,600
- Doctors of Geology.

528
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:28,833
We operate only with
little hammers on rocks.

529
00:23:28,833 --> 00:23:31,433
- [Joel] If you have kidney
stones we're the guys to call.

530
00:23:31,433 --> 00:23:33,933
- Lucero always goes
back to Miraflores.

531
00:23:33,933 --> 00:23:36,600
But the saddle, I don't know.

532
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:38,167
- I'll get it.

533
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:39,333
- You're very kind.

534
00:23:39,333 --> 00:23:41,067
- [Crow] No he's
not, I'm kinder.

535
00:23:41,067 --> 00:23:42,533
- Do you happen
to have a canteen?

536
00:23:42,533 --> 00:23:44,433
- Well sure right
on the Jeep come on.

537
00:23:51,267 --> 00:23:52,833
There's a mirror you can use.

538
00:23:52,833 --> 00:23:53,667
- Great.

539
00:23:57,867 --> 00:24:00,367
- We'll be here
several weeks at least.

540
00:24:00,367 --> 00:24:01,467
See we're conducting.

541
00:24:01,467 --> 00:24:03,267
- [Tom] Try a little of this.

542
00:24:03,267 --> 00:24:05,433
I made it myself,
it's my own sweat

543
00:24:05,433 --> 00:24:09,267
- You make it sound like a
very intriguing occupation.

544
00:24:09,267 --> 00:24:10,533
- [Tom] Well I didn't mean to.

545
00:24:10,533 --> 00:24:12,033
- It is, you meet such
interesting volcanoes.

546
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:13,500
- [Crow] And you're one of them.

547
00:24:15,067 --> 00:24:17,700
- [Joel] What do you know.

548
00:24:19,133 --> 00:24:21,267
Couple of rocks piled
on top of other rocks.

549
00:24:21,267 --> 00:24:22,333
That's kind of fishy.

550
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:25,367
Let's dig down a
little bit and yeah.

551
00:24:26,433 --> 00:24:27,267
What?

552
00:24:27,267 --> 00:24:28,333
"Thou shalt not ki."

553
00:24:29,567 --> 00:24:31,167
What?

554
00:24:31,167 --> 00:24:32,233
"Thou shalt not ki."

555
00:24:33,367 --> 00:24:35,033
Huh.

556
00:24:35,033 --> 00:24:36,700
I'll take that back.

557
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:38,400
Should make the saddle heavier.

558
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:40,067
- Hey Hank!

559
00:24:40,067 --> 00:24:41,000
- [Joel] Look at this!

560
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,267
It says "Thou shalt not ki."

561
00:24:43,267 --> 00:24:44,500
- Thank you doctor.

562
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:45,767
- [Joel] What do
you make of that?

563
00:24:45,767 --> 00:24:46,967
- [Tom] I guess we're
not supposed to "Ki".

564
00:24:46,967 --> 00:24:48,300
- I found this near the saddle.

565
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:49,233
- Oh is that good?

566
00:24:49,233 --> 00:24:50,800
- I'll say it is, it's obsidian.

567
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:53,033
- [Crow] Oh I don't
think it's that bad.

568
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,567
- Well I wouldn't know.

569
00:24:54,567 --> 00:24:56,533
Cattle yes but rocks.

570
00:24:56,533 --> 00:24:58,467
Could I ask another
favor of you?

571
00:24:58,467 --> 00:24:59,900
- [Joel] Can I
borrow some makeup?

572
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:00,900
- Would you mind turning back

573
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:02,300
and taking me to San Lorenzo?

574
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:03,567
- We'd be glad to.

575
00:25:03,567 --> 00:25:04,567
- Thank you.

576
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:09,400
- [Crow] Wow you'll do
anything for a chick.

577
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:11,000
- I must get there today.

578
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,900
- [Tom] Where'd you get
your hat block Dale?

579
00:25:12,900 --> 00:25:15,067
- Riders to help with my cattle.

580
00:25:15,067 --> 00:25:16,300
That old volcano is really

581
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:18,033
causing a lot of
trouble this time.

582
00:25:18,033 --> 00:25:20,733
- Yeah we heard in the
village about your cowboys.

583
00:25:20,733 --> 00:25:21,900
- Oh?

584
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:24,967
Well if I lose my cattle
I lose everything.

585
00:25:24,967 --> 00:25:26,367
How are things at Sal Lorenzo?

586
00:25:26,367 --> 00:25:28,233
- [Crow] Well the
Milling Festival is over

587
00:25:28,233 --> 00:25:29,867
ended in a weird steak fight.

588
00:25:29,867 --> 00:25:31,833
Found a baby though,
gave it to a priest.

589
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:34,700
And that pretty much sums up
where we are in the movie.

590
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:35,633
- [Tom] The weather
started getting

591
00:25:35,633 --> 00:25:37,200
rough the tiny ship was tossed.

592
00:25:38,700 --> 00:25:41,467
- Is that any reason to act
like frightened children?

593
00:25:41,467 --> 00:25:44,067
- I don't think it's just
a poisonous plant señorita.

594
00:25:44,067 --> 00:25:45,867
Even in this climate
you don't grow them

595
00:25:45,867 --> 00:25:48,700
that can push in the side of
a building and wreck a car.

596
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:49,900
- [Joel] Oh but we do.

597
00:25:49,900 --> 00:25:52,233
You're not from
around here are you?

598
00:25:52,233 --> 00:25:53,067
Strange man.

599
00:25:56,833 --> 00:25:59,033
- [Crow] The Milling
Festival over the citizens

600
00:25:59,033 --> 00:26:02,233
are loaded on to flatbed
trucks like so many cattle.

601
00:26:04,933 --> 00:26:06,400
- [Tom] Everybody don't "ki!"

602
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:08,800
- Oh don't forget.

603
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:10,100
You promised to use Miraflores
as your headquarters.

604
00:26:10,100 --> 00:26:12,200
- It will be a great
convenience señorita.

605
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:13,800
- Will it really?

606
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:14,600
- Right.

607
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:17,533
- [Joel] Hey Stevo
flip you for her.

608
00:26:18,733 --> 00:26:20,200
- [Tom] Hey you see my haircut?

609
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:21,767
Look I got a haircut too!

610
00:26:21,767 --> 00:26:24,500
Look haircut, haircut,
haircut, haircut, haircut.

611
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:25,867
We all got our haircut!

612
00:26:27,333 --> 00:26:31,533
(speaks in foreign language)

613
00:26:31,533 --> 00:26:33,033
All of you.

614
00:26:33,033 --> 00:26:34,733
Let me ask you this.

615
00:26:34,733 --> 00:26:35,667
- [Crow] Are those foam hats?

616
00:26:35,667 --> 00:26:37,233
I told you to wear mouse ears.

617
00:26:37,233 --> 00:26:38,900
- Would you have
become frightened

618
00:26:38,900 --> 00:26:40,433
of sounds in the night and run

619
00:26:40,433 --> 00:26:42,567
like silly children to
the safety of the village?

620
00:26:42,567 --> 00:26:44,700
- Yeah, absolutely.
- I would.

621
00:26:44,700 --> 00:26:46,100
- I say only this muchachos.

622
00:26:47,267 --> 00:26:49,600
I've known you all
for all my life.

623
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:51,033
We've always worked together.

624
00:26:51,033 --> 00:26:52,967
- [Joel] Me usually
bossing you around.

625
00:26:54,033 --> 00:26:55,567
- That's right.

626
00:26:55,567 --> 00:26:59,600
- If you don't wish to return
just to help me save my cattle

627
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:03,033
for me then, return
to save Miraflores.

628
00:27:05,467 --> 00:27:09,233
(speaks in foreign language)

629
00:27:09,233 --> 00:27:11,433
- [Joel] Looks like
the answer is no.

630
00:27:11,433 --> 00:27:12,267
- Gracias.

631
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:18,400
- [Tom] All right señors
back to my house for tacos.

632
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:19,867
Hats on.

633
00:27:19,867 --> 00:27:23,000
- Dr Scott, Mayor
Garcia wants to see you.

634
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:24,267
- Where is he?

635
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:25,800
- In the laboratory
with Dr De La Cruz.

636
00:27:25,800 --> 00:27:26,733
- Laboratory?

637
00:27:26,733 --> 00:27:27,667
- You'll be surprised by the

638
00:27:27,667 --> 00:27:29,000
experiments that go on there.

639
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,600
- [Crow] He's making
a taco salad where

640
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:33,133
you can actually eat the bowl!

641
00:27:33,133 --> 00:27:36,200
(upbeat theme music)

642
00:27:38,533 --> 00:27:40,967
- Doctor is that the patrolman?

643
00:27:43,133 --> 00:27:44,300
- Yes.

644
00:27:44,300 --> 00:27:46,333
Sergeant Vega.

645
00:27:46,333 --> 00:27:51,333
Relieved doing his duty now
who may perform a greater one.

646
00:27:51,933 --> 00:27:53,467
- [Tom] Ick.

647
00:27:53,467 --> 00:27:56,000
- [Joel] You see I deep fried
a small portion of soft shell

648
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,600
now look at the salsa
I mixed up here.

649
00:28:02,833 --> 00:28:05,633
- [Tom] They are flavor buds,
they are bursting with flavor!

650
00:28:05,633 --> 00:28:07,867
- Well?

651
00:28:07,867 --> 00:28:09,433
- Black subcutaneous cells that

652
00:28:09,433 --> 00:28:11,600
had just burst or run rampant.

653
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:14,567
- [Crow] So that salsa is
really really hot then right?

654
00:28:16,033 --> 00:28:20,733
- Not from any poison I can
identify with this equipment

655
00:28:22,733 --> 00:28:25,300
Lopez you help again please?

656
00:28:27,567 --> 00:28:29,933
- [Joel] Isn't that the
guy from The Eurythmics?

657
00:28:33,067 --> 00:28:34,700
- In this pure alcohol

658
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,400
and this distilled water

659
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:39,900
and this tequila.

660
00:28:39,900 --> 00:28:41,067
- [Tom] Ah that's for me.

661
00:28:41,067 --> 00:28:43,500
- And this water with some salt.

662
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:45,000
- [Crow] And then
bring some Shinola

663
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,900
and we'll compare it with
the last one I gave you.

664
00:28:46,900 --> 00:28:49,833
- Think it is a poison then?
- I do.

665
00:28:49,833 --> 00:28:51,800
- Not a chemical poison Doctor?

666
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:52,933
- No.

667
00:28:52,933 --> 00:28:55,300
But I believe for many reasons.

668
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:58,333
- [Joel] More like a paste
like I use in my hair.

669
00:28:58,333 --> 00:29:00,433
- I have had a little
experience with them.

670
00:29:00,433 --> 00:29:02,133
The venoms of the snakes.

671
00:29:02,133 --> 00:29:04,233
The wasps and spiders.

672
00:29:04,233 --> 00:29:07,667
But I will prepare the
slides and the specimens

673
00:29:07,667 --> 00:29:09,467
and take them to a
man in Mexico City

674
00:29:09,467 --> 00:29:11,133
who will be sure to know.

675
00:29:11,133 --> 00:29:13,067
- [Crow] Now do you
serve those with crackers

676
00:29:13,067 --> 00:29:15,600
or do you spread them on
those toasted garlic rounds?

677
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:17,933
- Well as you say if
it's an organic poison

678
00:29:17,933 --> 00:29:22,067
anything from nature the Great
Vilasko will identify it.

679
00:29:22,067 --> 00:29:24,967
- [Tom] The Great Vilasko,
juggler sword swallower

680
00:29:24,967 --> 00:29:26,867
and pathologist extraordinaire.

681
00:29:26,867 --> 00:29:29,733
- One wound here with no blood.

682
00:29:29,733 --> 00:29:33,033
Then the situation
of the tissues.

683
00:29:33,033 --> 00:29:35,467
The strange bacteria.

684
00:29:35,467 --> 00:29:39,767
Bacteria I think found
in the soil samples

685
00:29:39,767 --> 00:29:41,300
near the footprints.

686
00:29:41,300 --> 00:29:42,967
Footprints?
Footprints?

687
00:29:42,967 --> 00:29:44,400
- [Crow] What prints?

688
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:46,567
- Footprints.
- Footprints?

689
00:29:47,700 --> 00:29:50,000
- Where something
knocks down dwellings,

690
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:51,733
flattens cornfields.

691
00:29:51,733 --> 00:29:53,467
- [Crow] Now these
aren't actual footprints

692
00:29:53,467 --> 00:29:55,833
this is feta cheese
but it smells like feet

693
00:29:55,833 --> 00:29:57,633
and that's as close
as we could get.

694
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:02,767
- Whatever it is my friends
I don't believe anyone

695
00:30:02,767 --> 00:30:07,000
has ever seen a foot,
a claw, this size

696
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:10,933
except those poor unfortunates
who wish they never had.

697
00:30:10,933 --> 00:30:13,100
- One question Doctor.
- What?

698
00:30:13,100 --> 00:30:14,933
- I hope I can answer it.

699
00:30:14,933 --> 00:30:16,467
- The alcohol, the
distilled water,

700
00:30:16,467 --> 00:30:18,800
the salt solution, I
can understand that.

701
00:30:18,800 --> 00:30:21,700
- [Joel] It all makes a great
salad dressing doesn't it.

702
00:30:21,700 --> 00:30:24,567
- Well in your country I believe

703
00:30:24,567 --> 00:30:26,633
you call it a coffee break.

704
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,267
- [Crow] Hey let's
all grab a margarita

705
00:30:29,267 --> 00:30:31,500
and head out to my turtle
pool what do you say?

706
00:30:32,433 --> 00:30:35,200
- [Joel] Hey it's the big valley

707
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:36,667
and there's Barbara Stanwick.

708
00:30:46,867 --> 00:30:49,367
- [Crow] There goes the
surrey with the fringe on top.

709
00:30:51,767 --> 00:30:53,000
- [Tom] Don't forget the Alamo!

710
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:54,333
No wait, we can do better.

711
00:30:54,333 --> 00:30:55,833
Davey Crocker is a dork!

712
00:30:55,833 --> 00:30:56,800
No.

713
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,600
Remember the, oh forget it.

714
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:02,733
- Looks like you
were pretty lucky.

715
00:31:02,733 --> 00:31:04,633
That thing really
came close didn't it?

716
00:31:04,633 --> 00:31:05,867
- [Crow] Yeah it
used to be worse.

717
00:31:05,867 --> 00:31:07,100
- We were blessed that
it didn't go any further

718
00:31:07,100 --> 00:31:08,367
our plantation
would've been ruined

719
00:31:08,367 --> 00:31:09,967
like the rest of the land.

720
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:14,000
- [Joel] Makes a lot of sense.

721
00:31:19,433 --> 00:31:21,900
- [Tom] Meanwhile back at
Neighborville Illinois.

722
00:31:24,067 --> 00:31:25,933
- Señorita thank
heavens you're safe.

723
00:31:25,933 --> 00:31:26,767
- [Joel] Oh really?

724
00:31:26,767 --> 00:31:28,100
I was worried about you.

725
00:31:28,100 --> 00:31:30,367
- I began to search the hills.

726
00:31:30,367 --> 00:31:33,033
- Oh Peo I had already
been found by someone else.

727
00:31:33,033 --> 00:31:35,133
This is Dr Scott and Dr Ramos.

728
00:31:35,133 --> 00:31:37,133
This is my foreman Peo.

729
00:31:37,133 --> 00:31:37,967
- Hi Peo.

730
00:31:40,767 --> 00:31:42,033
- [Crow] Chump.

731
00:31:49,267 --> 00:31:51,667
- Not only comfortable
but cool too.

732
00:31:51,667 --> 00:31:53,067
- Yes sometimes I
think being cool

733
00:31:53,067 --> 00:31:55,667
is by far the most
important on days like this.

734
00:31:55,667 --> 00:31:57,333
Well I know you'll want showers.

735
00:31:57,333 --> 00:32:00,600
- [Joel] Wow it looks like
she lives at the Gala winery.

736
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:02,000
- Florentina.

737
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:03,633
Show Dr Ramos to the blue room?

738
00:32:03,633 --> 00:32:06,267
- [Crow] And then sponge
bathe our guests won't you?

739
00:32:06,267 --> 00:32:08,400
- Show Dr Scott
to the left wing.

740
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:09,633
- I'll take care of them!

741
00:32:12,567 --> 00:32:13,800
- Well I'll see you later

742
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:15,433
and you can tell me all
about your expedition.

743
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:16,967
- [Tom] You mean in the shower?

744
00:32:19,633 --> 00:32:20,833
- Not bad doc.

745
00:32:22,467 --> 00:32:24,067
- [Tom] Meanwhile in the shower.

746
00:32:25,600 --> 00:32:26,900
(cows moo)

747
00:32:26,900 --> 00:32:29,100
- Good day's work.
- Chalaco not bad.

748
00:32:29,100 --> 00:32:30,333
- [Joel] All right
everybody thank you

749
00:32:30,333 --> 00:32:32,600
but Oklahoma has
been cast already.

750
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:33,867
- By Thursday.

751
00:32:33,867 --> 00:32:36,767
Why put on such a face?

752
00:32:36,767 --> 00:32:38,667
We will do it if I have

753
00:32:38,667 --> 00:32:40,300
to stay in the saddle
without sleep myself.

754
00:32:40,300 --> 00:32:42,000
- You must understand
can't you see?

755
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,433
The cattle knows that something

756
00:32:43,433 --> 00:32:44,833
evil is carried on the wind.

757
00:32:45,833 --> 00:32:46,767
- [Crow] That's the cat.

758
00:32:46,767 --> 00:32:49,333
- Now let us have a good supper

759
00:32:49,333 --> 00:32:51,433
and forgot these superstitions.

760
00:32:51,433 --> 00:32:53,533
- [Joel] Hey quit
shouting back there!

761
