1010
00:44:37,267 --> 00:44:38,267
- [Tom] Just part of me.

1011
00:44:38,267 --> 00:44:39,767
- This is all that remains.

1012
00:44:39,767 --> 00:44:41,967
Even the animals.

1013
00:44:41,967 --> 00:44:44,500
I cannot speak of this night.

1014
00:44:44,500 --> 00:44:46,800
- [Tom] Well then just
don't speak of it.

1015
00:44:46,800 --> 00:44:48,733
- Father I have been
sent here in charge

1016
00:44:48,733 --> 00:44:50,467
of emergency arrangements.

1017
00:44:50,467 --> 00:44:52,633
All that are left will
be moved to safety.

1018
00:44:52,633 --> 00:44:55,967
Please tell everyone to be
ready to leave San Lorenzo.

1019
00:44:55,967 --> 00:44:58,300
And Father they
may only take what

1020
00:44:58,300 --> 00:44:59,767
they can carry in their arms.

1021
00:44:59,767 --> 00:45:01,167
- [Tom] I'm not your father.

1022
00:45:01,167 --> 00:45:02,767
- Where is the laboratory?
- Over there.

1023
00:45:05,367 --> 00:45:06,967
- [Crow] Is it
lavatory or Laboratory?

1024
00:45:06,967 --> 00:45:08,800
- As soon as I
received the samples

1025
00:45:08,800 --> 00:45:11,600
I identified the poison
is that of a scorpion.

1026
00:45:11,600 --> 00:45:13,100
But I had no concept of the

1027
00:45:13,100 --> 00:45:15,400
creature's size
until I saw this.

1028
00:45:15,400 --> 00:45:16,800
- [Joel] Your feta cheese?

1029
00:45:17,967 --> 00:45:20,133
- This specimen
found by Dr Ramos

1030
00:45:20,133 --> 00:45:24,500
is of a species thought to be
extinct as a Tri Asian Era.

1031
00:45:24,500 --> 00:45:25,933
- [Tom] As a what?

1032
00:45:25,933 --> 00:45:28,767
- We have known it in a
passive state but never alive.

1033
00:45:30,133 --> 00:45:31,933
Now from the bowels of the Earth

1034
00:45:31,933 --> 00:45:35,267
it has come forth again
to plague the Earth.

1035
00:45:35,267 --> 00:45:36,600
- What can we do?

1036
00:45:36,600 --> 00:45:39,200
I emptied the machine
gun on one of them.

1037
00:45:39,200 --> 00:45:41,700
- I beg of you all
not to lose your head.

1038
00:45:41,700 --> 00:45:45,033
- [Joel] Have you tried
reasoning to them?

1039
00:45:45,033 --> 00:45:46,967
- We have a few advantages
against this enemy.

1040
00:45:46,967 --> 00:45:49,333
- [Tom] First we're
small, we can run fast.

1041
00:45:50,467 --> 00:45:51,833
- Thus we have
the daylight hours

1042
00:45:51,833 --> 00:45:53,800
to try to find and destroy them.

1043
00:45:53,800 --> 00:45:57,333
Secondly they're somewhat
slow and lethargic.

1044
00:45:57,333 --> 00:45:59,800
- [Crow] And we have
giant 40 foot pinchers.

1045
00:45:59,800 --> 00:46:02,067
No wait that's the scorpions.

1046
00:46:02,067 --> 00:46:03,633
- One question sir.
- Yes?

1047
00:46:03,633 --> 00:46:06,033
- What weapon to do
you intend to use?

1048
00:46:06,033 --> 00:46:07,500
- Gas.

1049
00:46:07,500 --> 00:46:09,167
- [Tom] We're in Mexico
that should be easy to find.

1050
00:46:09,167 --> 00:46:11,767
- It has been proved effective
against normal species

1051
00:46:11,767 --> 00:46:13,667
let us pray it works against.

1052
00:46:13,667 --> 00:46:14,867
- [Tom] Enormous pieces?

1053
00:46:16,633 --> 00:46:17,833
- If it does not?

1054
00:46:17,833 --> 00:46:19,533
- [Crow] We give up and die.

1055
00:46:19,533 --> 00:46:21,233
- May God help all of you.

1056
00:46:23,867 --> 00:46:25,533
- [Tom] Or some of you.

1057
00:46:25,533 --> 00:46:27,067
Like you.

1058
00:46:27,067 --> 00:46:29,067
- [Joel] Okay Milling
Festival's over,

1059
00:46:29,067 --> 00:46:30,167
it's the Big Hat Fest.

1060
00:46:33,900 --> 00:46:35,700
- I want to do what I can too.

1061
00:46:35,700 --> 00:46:38,100
- Señorita Alvares I
understand your emotions.

1062
00:46:38,100 --> 00:46:40,100
- Believe me Dr Vilasko I'm
not trying to be emotional.

1063
00:46:40,100 --> 00:46:42,500
I wouldn't ask to come along
if I thought I couldn't help.

1064
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:43,900
- Teresa you don't
know the hardships.

1065
00:46:43,900 --> 00:46:45,500
- Dr Vilasko, Major Cocio,

1066
00:46:45,500 --> 00:46:48,567
I know this area like
the palm of my hand.

1067
00:46:48,567 --> 00:46:51,300
- [Tom] But she can't ride
a horse to save her life.

1068
00:46:51,300 --> 00:46:52,833
- I'm a good shot.

1069
00:46:52,833 --> 00:46:55,133
You said yourself you needed
all the help you could get.

1070
00:46:55,133 --> 00:47:00,200
- Señorita Alvares, I think
you have found yourself a job.

1071
00:47:01,567 --> 00:47:03,100
- [Crow] The pay's rotten
but the hours stink.

1072
00:47:04,900 --> 00:47:07,600
- Major Cocio and I
are planning this.

1073
00:47:07,600 --> 00:47:09,000
- [Joel] See I got
this lake property

1074
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:11,567
and it goes all the
way back to the woods.

1075
00:47:11,567 --> 00:47:12,767
- I want to go with you.

1076
00:47:12,767 --> 00:47:14,667
I want to do a job.

1077
00:47:14,667 --> 00:47:17,633
- Don't worry Juanito,
we'll get together again.

1078
00:47:17,633 --> 00:47:19,433
That's a promise.

1079
00:47:19,433 --> 00:47:22,400
See if you can find my
boots for me will you?

1080
00:47:22,400 --> 00:47:24,600
- I know where they are!

1081
00:47:24,600 --> 00:47:27,300
- [Crow] Oh they stink.

1082
00:47:27,300 --> 00:47:30,333
Hey did you actually
pay for these?

1083
00:47:31,267 --> 00:47:32,967
- [Joel] Line please.

1084
00:47:32,967 --> 00:47:34,400
- Here they are.

1085
00:47:34,400 --> 00:47:35,900
- Oh good!

1086
00:47:35,900 --> 00:47:38,267
- [Crow] Now stop eyeballing
them kid and give them to me.

1087
00:47:38,267 --> 00:47:40,233
- Kinda like those huh?

1088
00:47:40,233 --> 00:47:44,633
Tell you what Juanito when
you get to be a big man

1089
00:47:44,633 --> 00:47:47,400
I'll get you a pair
just like these.

1090
00:47:47,400 --> 00:47:48,567
- [Joel] No thanks.

1091
00:47:48,567 --> 00:47:50,000
- Thank you Mr Hank!

1092
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:51,067
- You like that huh?

1093
00:47:51,067 --> 00:47:53,033
- I know how to ride very good.

1094
00:47:53,033 --> 00:47:55,300
I know how to shoot very good.

1095
00:47:55,300 --> 00:47:56,300
- [Crow] Yeah yeah
we know you're

1096
00:47:56,300 --> 00:47:58,233
superboy too bad you can't act.

1097
00:47:58,233 --> 00:48:00,100
Hey can I call you Gary?

1098
00:48:02,033 --> 00:48:03,467
- Ah Juanito.

1099
00:48:03,467 --> 00:48:05,867
You know sometimes
even a half a man

1100
00:48:05,867 --> 00:48:08,133
has a lot of
different jobs to do.

1101
00:48:08,133 --> 00:48:10,267
And right now the most
important job for you to do

1102
00:48:10,267 --> 00:48:12,067
is to take care of
your grandmother.

1103
00:48:12,067 --> 00:48:13,867
- She can take care of herself!

1104
00:48:13,867 --> 00:48:15,233
- [Tom] Off her Juan
you'll be paid well for it.

1105
00:48:15,233 --> 00:48:16,933
- You've got plenty of time

1106
00:48:16,933 --> 00:48:18,533
to do more exciting things.

1107
00:48:18,533 --> 00:48:20,033
- And you?

1108
00:48:20,033 --> 00:48:22,367
You be very careful and
don't get hurt won't you?

1109
00:48:22,367 --> 00:48:23,767
- [Tom] You work on your diction

1110
00:48:23,767 --> 00:48:25,567
I'll catch up with you later.

1111
00:48:25,567 --> 00:48:29,033
- [Joel] Yeah that's
what Shane said.

1112
00:48:29,033 --> 00:48:29,867
- Okay.

1113
00:48:33,967 --> 00:48:35,700
- [Tom] Here they
are the 15th fairway.

1114
00:48:35,700 --> 00:48:38,500
Boy I wish they'd keep those
horses away from the green.

1115
00:48:42,200 --> 00:48:46,633
- I don't see a thing Dr
Vilasko, might as well go on.

1116
00:48:46,633 --> 00:48:47,467
- All right.

1117
00:48:52,600 --> 00:48:54,067
- [Crow] You playing the
Top Flight Five aren't you?

1118
00:48:54,067 --> 00:48:56,567
I usually use range balls
out here in the rough.

1119
00:48:56,567 --> 00:48:58,633
- [Joel] They're playing
the volcano hole.

1120
00:48:58,633 --> 00:49:00,933
Next is the windmill
and that's really tough.

1121
00:49:02,300 --> 00:49:03,900
- [Tom] Looks like he's gonna
use an iron on this one.

1122
00:49:03,900 --> 00:49:05,567
A little hard to believe
but he's been having

1123
00:49:05,567 --> 00:49:08,100
a lot of trouble with
his driver and his woods.

1124
00:49:08,100 --> 00:49:09,967
Looks like he's going
for a tough par.

1125
00:49:11,233 --> 00:49:13,367
Hey he was in our
foursome last week!

1126
00:49:13,367 --> 00:49:14,767
This is a rough hole.

1127
00:49:22,700 --> 00:49:23,900
- Major.

1128
00:49:25,267 --> 00:49:26,700
- Yes Doctor?

1129
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:28,100
- Tell your captain
to hold all the

1130
00:49:28,100 --> 00:49:29,667
heavy equipment
until we call for it.

1131
00:49:29,667 --> 00:49:31,000
- [Tom] You mean the irons?

1132
00:49:40,667 --> 00:49:41,667
- Look at this!

1133
00:49:41,667 --> 00:49:42,900
A great big opening!

1134
00:49:42,900 --> 00:49:44,567
- [Joel] Here's
the pit everybody!

1135
00:49:47,500 --> 00:49:48,500
- [Crow] Wow it is tough.

1136
00:49:48,500 --> 00:49:50,800
He's got to four
caddy that hole.

1137
00:49:50,800 --> 00:49:52,400
- Look there's something
wrong with his horse!

1138
00:49:52,400 --> 00:49:53,667
He's falling in!

1139
00:49:53,667 --> 00:49:55,033
- [Joel] No actors
were abused in the

1140
00:49:55,033 --> 00:49:56,567
making of this motion picture.

1141
00:49:59,700 --> 00:50:01,633
- [Crow] That's gonna
cost them a stroke

1142
00:50:04,533 --> 00:50:06,267
- [Tom] Take a full swing!

1143
00:50:10,067 --> 00:50:12,700
- We must get down
to the lower level.

1144
00:50:14,333 --> 00:50:15,533
- [Crow] The lady's tee?

1145
00:50:16,900 --> 00:50:19,633
(dramatic music)

1146
00:50:25,933 --> 00:50:27,867
Okay who has the orange ball?

1147
00:50:35,167 --> 00:50:36,967
- [Joel] Hey they moved the pin!

1148
00:50:40,600 --> 00:50:41,900
- This crevice is new.

1149
00:50:41,900 --> 00:50:44,200
It must've opened during
one of the earthquakes.

1150
00:50:44,200 --> 00:50:46,567
This looks like
a job for us Doc.

1151
00:50:46,567 --> 00:50:47,400
- Of course.

1152
00:50:47,400 --> 00:50:48,200
- No transport?

1153
00:50:50,333 --> 00:50:52,400
How deep do you say it is?

1154
00:50:52,400 --> 00:50:54,067
- Well Doc and I've
been down many a cave

1155
00:50:54,067 --> 00:50:55,433
but there's no way
of really telling.

1156
00:50:55,433 --> 00:50:57,033
- [Joel] I think it cuts
down into the right,

1157
00:50:57,033 --> 00:50:59,000
we should be able to bogey it.

1158
00:51:06,200 --> 00:51:07,300
Hey cut it out!

1159
00:51:07,300 --> 00:51:08,233
Ouch!

1160
00:51:13,600 --> 00:51:15,300
- Well the only
way we can find out

1161
00:51:15,300 --> 00:51:16,800
is try to go down
there ourselves.

1162
00:51:16,800 --> 00:51:17,733
What do you say Doc?

1163
00:51:17,733 --> 00:51:19,233
- [Joel] What are you high?

1164
00:51:19,233 --> 00:51:21,467
- Would that poisonous gas
work in a crevice this big?

1165
00:51:21,467 --> 00:51:23,533
- I could not anticipate
such a void as this.

1166
00:51:23,533 --> 00:51:26,200
- [Joel] I'm not a
big enough crevice.

1167
00:51:26,200 --> 00:51:27,400
- Major I think you better bring

1168
00:51:27,400 --> 00:51:28,933
all your heavy
equipment up here.

1169
00:51:28,933 --> 00:51:30,033
Crane tanks and all.

1170
00:51:32,567 --> 00:51:36,000
- Captain bring the crane
and all the heavy equipment.

1171
00:51:37,233 --> 00:51:39,100
You want my men
to go down there?

1172
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:41,467
It is suicide.

1173
00:51:41,467 --> 00:51:43,000
- Don't worry about it.

1174
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:44,933
Doc and I haven't had a decent
elevator ride in a long time.

1175
00:51:44,933 --> 00:51:46,700
- [Tom] We commit
suicide every day.

1176
00:51:48,533 --> 00:51:49,833
Got my snowmobile here.

1177
00:51:49,833 --> 00:51:51,267
Sno Cat really a beauty.

1178
00:51:52,300 --> 00:51:53,467
- What are you doing here?

1179
00:51:53,467 --> 00:51:54,800
- I'm a stowaway!

1180
00:51:54,800 --> 00:51:56,933
- [Joel] No you're
a volunteer kid.

1181
00:51:56,933 --> 00:51:58,167
- Do me a favor will you?

1182
00:51:58,167 --> 00:51:59,900
And just stay out of the way.

1183
00:51:59,900 --> 00:52:00,900
- Yes Mr Hank.

1184
00:52:00,900 --> 00:52:02,100
- Good.

1185
00:52:02,100 --> 00:52:03,600
And just sit in the Jeep
like a big boy okay?

1186
00:52:03,600 --> 00:52:05,633
- [Joel] Yeah wear that
checkerboard bib overalls

1187
00:52:05,633 --> 00:52:07,733
and hold a big sloppy
hamburger like that.

1188
00:52:10,067 --> 00:52:11,533
- Why the birds professor?

1189
00:52:11,533 --> 00:52:13,167
- Because if the
birds stop singing

1190
00:52:13,167 --> 00:52:15,200
that means there's
poison gas in the cave.

1191
00:52:15,200 --> 00:52:17,000
- [Crow] Fine time
to go jousting.

1192
00:52:17,000 --> 00:52:19,467
- Neither of you, it's
not your responsibility.

1193
00:52:19,467 --> 00:52:21,167
- Who's responsibility is it?

1194
00:52:21,167 --> 00:52:22,700
- [All] The producers.

1195
00:52:22,700 --> 00:52:23,633
- The army.

1196
00:52:23,633 --> 00:52:24,867
The people who live here!

1197
00:52:24,867 --> 00:52:26,600
- Now look Doc and I
know more about caves

1198
00:52:26,600 --> 00:52:27,767
than anyone else here.

1199
00:52:29,233 --> 00:52:30,633
- [Tom] Give me my gum back.

1200
00:52:31,767 --> 00:52:32,600
Thank you.

1201
00:52:32,600 --> 00:52:33,533
- [Joel] No you got it.

1202
00:52:33,533 --> 00:52:34,633
Here I want you to have it.

1203
00:52:38,300 --> 00:52:40,333
- Why did you do that?

1204
00:52:40,333 --> 00:52:42,900
- Maybe I just wanted
to see what you'd do?

1205
00:52:44,100 --> 00:52:45,667
- What did I do?

1206
00:52:45,667 --> 00:52:47,633
- [Crow] Well I don't
know but you did it first.

1207
00:52:47,633 --> 00:52:48,533
- Señorita.

1208
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:50,733
You can help us if you will

1209
00:52:50,733 --> 00:52:52,267
keep the log of the descent.

1210
00:52:52,267 --> 00:52:54,967
How many meters down, the
reports which are made.

1211
00:52:54,967 --> 00:52:58,000
- Sure, keep yourself
busy, that's my theory.

1212
00:52:58,000 --> 00:53:00,400
Oh don't forget take
care of little Juanito.

1213
00:53:00,400 --> 00:53:01,567
- [Joel] Juanito?

1214
00:53:01,567 --> 00:53:02,833
Oh you mean my kid!

1215
00:53:03,933 --> 00:53:06,667
(dramatic music)

1216
00:53:15,600 --> 00:53:18,000
- [Crow] And so
we enter the cage

1217
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:20,733
knowing the Earth's fiercest
creatures await us below.

1218
00:53:23,433 --> 00:53:24,267
Zsa Zsa.

1219
00:53:26,900 --> 00:53:28,100
- [Joel] He said down.

1220
00:53:29,867 --> 00:53:32,600
(dramatic music)

1221
00:53:39,200 --> 00:53:41,300
- [Crow] Lower and
lower we go traveling

1222
00:53:41,300 --> 00:53:43,100
past the matte paintings.

1223
00:53:48,933 --> 00:53:52,333
- [Tom] We suffer from the
banes of nitrogen narcosis.

1224
00:54:04,033 --> 00:54:05,300
- [Joel] I think
we're gonna need

1225
00:54:05,300 --> 00:54:07,333
a lot bigger boat you guys.

1226
00:54:07,333 --> 00:54:08,833
- [Crow] Should I get the cops?

1227
00:54:08,833 --> 00:54:10,767
I'll get the cops.

1228
00:54:10,767 --> 00:54:12,267
- Look down there.

1229
00:54:15,933 --> 00:54:17,300
- [Tom] Hello stop cage!

1230
00:54:17,300 --> 00:54:18,833
Big crab!

1231
00:54:18,833 --> 00:54:20,000
Big guy!

1232
00:54:20,000 --> 00:54:21,067
Oh boy!

1233
00:54:21,067 --> 00:54:22,067
Oh boy!

1234
00:54:22,067 --> 00:54:23,100
Bring us up!

1235
00:54:23,100 --> 00:54:24,367
Stop the cage!

1236
00:54:24,367 --> 00:54:27,167
- [Crow] Send down a
little lemon butter.

1237
00:54:27,167 --> 00:54:28,733
- Hold on a second.

1238
00:54:30,200 --> 00:54:32,300
- [Joel] Hal why don't
you go down there

1239
00:54:32,300 --> 00:54:33,467
and stand next to the creature

1240
00:54:33,467 --> 00:54:35,000
so I can get a sense of scale?

1241
00:54:38,533 --> 00:54:40,900
- Okay I got a picture of it.

1242
00:54:40,900 --> 00:54:41,933
Lower on.

1243
00:54:41,933 --> 00:54:43,333
- All right lower them down.

1244
00:54:44,733 --> 00:54:45,633
- [Tom] Down did I say down?

1245
00:54:45,633 --> 00:54:46,500
Up, I meant up.

1246
00:54:49,967 --> 00:54:52,900
He's gonna clip that
line like a nose hair.

1247
00:55:01,567 --> 00:55:05,567
- [Joel] Hey look over there
it says Arnie Sacknessen.

1248
00:55:05,567 --> 00:55:07,467
- [Crow] Deeper
and deeper we went

1249
00:55:07,467 --> 00:55:11,000
until our little thread was
all the way down you know.

1250
00:55:12,700 --> 00:55:16,100
- A huge cavern, I've never
seen a cave so big in my life.

1251
00:55:16,100 --> 00:55:18,767
- Can you see the
signs of Mendoza?

1252
00:55:18,767 --> 00:55:19,700
- No not from here.

1253
00:55:20,600 --> 00:55:22,100
We'll take a look around.

1254
00:55:28,667 --> 00:55:30,500
- [Joel] Seems like
a nice enough place.

1255
00:55:30,500 --> 00:55:31,467
- [Tom] At first.

1256
00:55:32,667 --> 00:55:34,933
- [Crow] We step
to see if it's cold

1257
00:55:34,933 --> 00:55:38,900
and lifeless when actually
it is teeming with life.

1258
00:55:38,900 --> 00:55:41,267
Here we see a sea anemone.

1259
00:55:41,267 --> 00:55:43,000
It's seemingly fragile structure

1260
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:44,967
adapted to the
massive pressures.

1261
00:55:44,967 --> 00:55:46,600
At this depth the sea pressure

1262
00:55:46,600 --> 00:55:49,167
could crush a man's
head like a pimple.

1263
00:55:59,100 --> 00:56:00,767
- [Joel] Hey Chirpy.

1264
00:56:07,267 --> 00:56:09,000
- [Tom] Is this Dune?

1265
00:56:11,433 --> 00:56:13,000
- [Crow] Here we see
one of the beautiful

1266
00:56:13,000 --> 00:56:15,067
creatures of the sea floor.

1267
00:56:15,067 --> 00:56:18,300
Though it appears vicious to
the eye it is very docile.

1268
00:56:18,300 --> 00:56:19,800
You can see the creature's lure

1269
00:56:19,800 --> 00:56:22,300
which is a lump of flesh
in front of the ink sack.

1270
00:56:25,600 --> 00:56:26,600
- [Joel] Well this
is the winner of

1271
00:56:26,600 --> 00:56:28,533
the Uniroyal Pioneer Trophy.

1272
00:56:28,533 --> 00:56:30,533
Now this float is called
The Little Inchworm.

1273
00:56:30,533 --> 00:56:31,933
It's made entirely out of

1274
00:56:31,933 --> 00:56:34,000
white coral flowers
and dried shellfish.

1275
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:35,233
It's a real piece of work.

1276
00:56:35,233 --> 00:56:36,067
Kathy Lee?

1277
00:56:37,700 --> 00:56:38,867
- Hank answer!

1278
00:56:48,700 --> 00:56:50,633
- [Crow] Hey he
likes to wear hats.

1279
00:56:50,633 --> 00:56:52,433
We just find a bug that can wear

1280
00:56:52,433 --> 00:56:54,500
this hat and we've got our man.

1281
00:56:54,500 --> 00:56:56,500
- Or their worm.
- Exactly.

1282
00:56:57,500 --> 00:56:58,767
- Are you there Hank?

1283
00:57:01,967 --> 00:57:03,200
Dr Ramos.

1284
00:57:03,200 --> 00:57:04,033
Dr Ramos.

1285
00:57:08,233 --> 00:57:10,500
- [Tom] Elven boy hid
behind the gas tanks.

1286
00:57:15,533 --> 00:57:16,600
- Hello, hello?

1287
00:57:17,767 --> 00:57:20,867
- Hello!
- Damn these Sprint lines!

1288
00:57:20,867 --> 00:57:22,300
- Yes?

1289
00:57:22,300 --> 00:57:23,133
- Mendoza's dead.

1290
00:57:28,133 --> 00:57:30,200
- We just saw a
worm 30 feet long.

1291
00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:32,067
- [Crow] And boy
does it catch fish.

1292
00:57:32,067 --> 00:57:34,700
- We want to look around
a little more first.

1293
00:57:43,300 --> 00:57:44,133
- Hey Doc!

1294
00:57:44,133 --> 00:57:45,133
- Over here!

1295
00:57:46,333 --> 00:57:49,033
- [Tom] There's a
big set over here!

1296
00:57:49,033 --> 00:57:50,200
Over here, over here.

1297
00:57:50,200 --> 00:57:51,400
- [Joel] Stay down Sabu.

1298
00:57:57,100 --> 00:57:58,267
Aw yuck, look out.

1299
00:57:59,867 --> 00:58:04,867
♪ The ants go marching
one by one hurrah hurrah ♪

1300
00:58:06,033 --> 00:58:08,633
- There must be
a nest somewhere.

1301
00:58:10,767 --> 00:58:12,533
♪ The ants go
marching one by one ♪

1302
00:58:12,533 --> 00:58:16,933
♪ The humans stopped
to shoot a gun ♪

1303
00:58:16,933 --> 00:58:18,433
- Doesn't even penetrate it.

1304
00:58:18,433 --> 00:58:19,933
- Try another one.

1305
00:58:25,967 --> 00:58:27,300
- [Crow] Better call Orkin.

1306
00:58:28,867 --> 00:58:30,500
Or throw the boy at them.

1307
00:58:35,667 --> 00:58:38,367
- [Joel] Yep these are
scorpion prints all right.

1308
00:58:50,633 --> 00:58:52,600
- [Tom] Are they in the
basement of the volcano,

1309
00:58:52,600 --> 00:58:53,467
is that the deal?

1310
00:58:55,133 --> 00:58:57,867
(dramatic music)

1311
00:58:59,367 --> 00:59:01,667
- [Crow] Made him
mad, not a good thing.

1312
00:59:08,567 --> 00:59:10,033
- [Joel] You know even
if they catch that thing.

1313
00:59:10,033 --> 00:59:13,067
they're gonna need a lemon
the size of a Volvo to eat it.

1314
00:59:24,367 --> 00:59:27,467
- [Crow] I think I'll go
make some yummy curry sauce.

1315
00:59:27,467 --> 00:59:28,333
With my own body.

1316
00:59:29,367 --> 00:59:30,533
- [Tom] Becky?

1317
00:59:30,533 --> 00:59:32,033
Engine Joe?

1318
00:59:32,033 --> 00:59:32,867
Huck?

1319
00:59:39,667 --> 00:59:41,200
- [Joel] Let's knock
off for the day Bill.

1320
00:59:41,200 --> 00:59:42,333
It's been a long one and I sure

1321
00:59:42,333 --> 00:59:45,200
could go for a nice cold brew.

1322
00:59:45,200 --> 00:59:47,000
Scorpions like this always keep

1323
00:59:47,000 --> 00:59:49,167
lots of ice cold beer around.

1324
00:59:50,900 --> 00:59:53,633
- [Crow] Sounds like there's
an opera going on next door.

1325
01:00:02,133 --> 01:00:03,067
- [Joel] I got 20
bucks that says the

1326
01:00:03,067 --> 01:00:05,167
scorpion who wins this one.

1327
01:00:05,167 --> 01:00:06,833
- [Tom] I'm just
plain terrified.

1328
01:00:09,367 --> 01:00:11,700
(screeches)

1329
01:00:27,533 --> 01:00:28,967
Well he's got a foreign object.

1330
01:00:28,967 --> 01:00:33,000
Well Carmel I can't believe
what I'm seeing here.

1331
01:00:41,667 --> 01:00:44,100
- [Crow] What does it smell
like in here to you guys?

1332
01:00:46,367 --> 01:00:48,667
(screeches)

1333
01:01:02,500 --> 01:01:03,900
- Yuck.
- Growdy.

1334
01:01:05,200 --> 01:01:06,400
- Must be the
grandaddy of them all

1335
01:01:06,400 --> 01:01:07,667
- [Crow] Wilford Brimley?

1336
01:01:09,767 --> 01:01:12,433
- [Joel] Good make sure they
can see us, thanks a lot.

1337
01:01:23,967 --> 01:01:24,900
- That's how they
kill each other,

1338
01:01:24,900 --> 01:01:26,733
that weak spot in the throat.

1339
01:01:26,733 --> 01:01:28,167
- [Tom] Good eye.

1340
01:01:29,800 --> 01:01:32,433
- [Crow] Go out there and
strangle them will you Hal?

1341
01:01:35,433 --> 01:01:38,200
(dramatic music)

1342
01:01:54,633 --> 01:01:57,267
- [Tom] Oh great
it's a wood tick.

1343
01:01:57,267 --> 01:01:59,233
He's gonna get
Lyme's disease now!

1344
01:01:59,233 --> 01:02:00,967
- [Crow] Quick get
a lit cigarette!

1345
01:02:01,933 --> 01:02:02,767
- Help!

1346
01:02:04,000 --> 01:02:05,500
Help!

1347
01:02:05,500 --> 01:02:08,200
- [Joel] That doesn't sound
like a giant mutated scorpion.

1348
01:02:09,333 --> 01:02:10,800
- [Tom] Come on afraid
of a little tick?

1349
01:02:10,800 --> 01:02:12,633
You little pansy.

1350
01:02:12,633 --> 01:02:13,467
- Help!

1351
01:02:15,400 --> 01:02:16,633
Help!

1352
01:02:16,633 --> 01:02:17,467
Help!

1353
01:02:24,400 --> 01:02:25,867
- [Tom] Juanito come back!

1354
01:02:30,967 --> 01:02:34,033
(upbeat theme music)

1355
01:02:37,933 --> 01:02:39,900
- [Hank] Stay back
in the cave Juanito!

1356
01:02:39,900 --> 01:02:42,300
- [Crow] Because you got
some explaining to do boy.

1357
01:02:48,867 --> 01:02:51,767
- [Joel] Let's get some Deep
Woods OFF and finish him off.

1358
01:02:52,967 --> 01:02:55,000
- I thought I told you
to stay in the Jeep.

1359
01:02:55,000 --> 01:02:56,233
what are you doing down here?

1360
01:02:56,233 --> 01:02:58,200
- I came to help you.
- You knucklehead.

1361
01:02:58,200 --> 01:02:59,000
- To help us?

1362
01:03:00,700 --> 01:03:03,067
No come on.

1363
01:03:03,067 --> 01:03:04,967
- [Tom] All right
you're bait come on.

1364
01:03:23,933 --> 01:03:25,800
Holy buckets.

1365
01:03:25,800 --> 01:03:27,267
- Mr Hank, Mr Hank!

1366
01:03:27,267 --> 01:03:28,100
Look!

1367
01:03:34,033 --> 01:03:35,367
- [Joel] Oh well
this isn't good.

1368
01:03:35,367 --> 01:03:36,967
Not at all.

1369
01:03:36,967 --> 01:03:38,167
I mean I've seen good before

1370
01:03:38,167 --> 01:03:39,300
and it didn't look
anything this.

1371
01:03:39,300 --> 01:03:40,900
Remember that bad thing we saw?

1372
01:03:40,900 --> 01:03:43,067
Well it looked
like this remember?

1373
01:03:43,067 --> 01:03:44,433
Definitely bad.

1374
01:03:50,367 --> 01:03:54,567
- [Tom] That scorpion really
wants to use that phone booth.

1375
01:03:54,567 --> 01:03:56,400
- [Crow] Okay play
him out a little.

1376
01:03:57,300 --> 01:03:58,567
Keep your rocked hip high.

1377
01:04:00,233 --> 01:04:01,900
And when you're
ready set the hook.

1378
01:04:08,167 --> 01:04:10,067
- The crane will be pulled in!

1379
01:04:10,067 --> 01:04:12,033
- Throw some rocks
under that crane!

1380
01:04:12,033 --> 01:04:13,767
- [Tom] No you do it.

1381
01:04:18,233 --> 01:04:20,600
- There goes our cage,
gas tanks, everything.

1382
01:04:20,600 --> 01:04:22,033
- [Joel] And my
lunch was in there!

1383
01:04:23,833 --> 01:04:26,567
(dramatic music)

1384
01:04:32,167 --> 01:04:37,167
- [Tom] Come here you!

1385
01:04:41,033 --> 01:04:42,200
- [Joel] Yuck.

1386
01:04:45,633 --> 01:04:46,867
- [Crow] Great we lost 'em.

1387
01:04:46,867 --> 01:04:49,567
He went under the boat,
now we're out of bait

1388
01:04:49,567 --> 01:04:51,000
- Here take the cable Doc,

1389
01:04:51,000 --> 01:04:53,133
and send it back out
as fast as we can.

1390
01:04:53,133 --> 01:04:54,100
- Bring it in slow.

1391
01:05:00,567 --> 01:05:01,700
- Maybe they're on it?

1392
01:05:01,700 --> 01:05:02,533
- Oh pull it up.

1393
01:05:02,533 --> 01:05:03,367
Please pull it up!

1394
01:05:03,367 --> 01:05:04,200
- Keep bringing it in.

1395
01:05:07,133 --> 01:05:10,200
- [Joel] Just keep thinking
about your happy thoughts,

1396
01:05:10,200 --> 01:05:12,100
don't look down.

1397
01:05:12,100 --> 01:05:14,133
I know you're a bendy
doll in this scene.

1398
01:05:15,333 --> 01:05:16,167
Don't give up.

1399
01:05:20,200 --> 01:05:21,433
- Come on, hold on!

1400
01:05:21,433 --> 01:05:22,900
- [Tom] I bet you
couldn't even climb

1401
01:05:22,900 --> 01:05:23,833
the rope in high
school could you?

1402
01:05:23,833 --> 01:05:24,567
You gutless wonder, you wimp!

1403
01:05:30,800 --> 01:05:32,867
Get me I'm a bendy doll.

1404
01:05:34,433 --> 01:05:36,533
Higher and higher he goes.

1405
01:05:38,367 --> 01:05:41,000
He's getting a nosebleed.

1406
01:05:41,000 --> 01:05:43,767
(dramatic music)

1407
01:05:56,000 --> 01:05:57,400
- [Joel] Well how was it?

1408
01:06:06,133 --> 01:06:08,867
- [Crow] By this time my
lungs were aching for air.

1409
01:06:09,767 --> 01:06:11,000
- What happened to Hank?

1410
01:06:11,000 --> 01:06:12,200
- Hank and Juanito
are down there too.

1411
01:06:12,200 --> 01:06:14,900
Get a loop on the cable
send it down quick!

1412
01:06:14,900 --> 01:06:16,467
- Make a loop on the cable!

1413
01:06:16,467 --> 01:06:17,867
- [Joel] Loopy on the cable.

1414
01:06:19,300 --> 01:06:22,067
(dramatic music)

1415
01:06:29,267 --> 01:06:32,033
Okay now get a shot
of me with the buck.

1416
01:06:34,133 --> 01:06:35,767
Make a real good pose there.

1417
01:06:38,867 --> 01:06:42,133
- [Crow] Oh I'll send the rope
back down for you I promise.

1418
01:06:42,133 --> 01:06:43,733
By the way can I have your bike?

1419
01:06:44,900 --> 01:06:46,700
- [Tom] Great he's
a human piñata now.

1420
01:06:46,700 --> 01:06:47,733
Darn darn darn!

1421
01:06:48,933 --> 01:06:51,667
(dramatic music)

1422
01:06:58,200 --> 01:07:01,000
- [Joel] Grab a Mountain Dew
and try that, it's a blast.

1423
01:07:07,133 --> 01:07:08,300
- Oh Juanito.

1424
01:07:08,300 --> 01:07:10,433
Oh Juanito why did you do it?

1425
01:07:10,433 --> 01:07:12,367
- [Tom] We are engaged.

1426
01:07:14,100 --> 01:07:15,700
- It'll be dark in about an hour

1427
01:07:15,700 --> 01:07:17,833
and those scorpions will
be coming out again.

1428
01:07:17,833 --> 01:07:19,100
- You couldn't use the gas?

1429
01:07:19,100 --> 01:07:21,267
- No we lost it in
the molten lava.

1430
01:07:21,267 --> 01:07:23,200
There must be about 50 of
those things down there.

1431
01:07:23,200 --> 01:07:26,067
- Can't we close that opening
with dynamite and seal it?

1432
01:07:26,067 --> 01:07:28,500
- You have no idea as to
the size of that place.

1433
01:07:28,500 --> 01:07:30,233
Wait until you see
these pictures.

1434
01:07:30,233 --> 01:07:32,800
- [Crow] They're great,
remember corn palace last year?

1435
01:07:32,800 --> 01:07:33,967
Even better than that!

1436
01:07:33,967 --> 01:07:36,400
Oops I left the lens cap on.

1437
01:07:36,400 --> 01:07:39,800
- Major we must try to seal
it shut with an explosion.

1438
01:07:39,800 --> 01:07:41,600
We must start before nightfall.

1439
01:07:43,033 --> 01:07:43,867
- [Tom] Okay.

1440
01:07:46,867 --> 01:07:49,167
- [Crow] So there was a
hook on the door handle.

1441
01:07:49,167 --> 01:07:50,400
Scary.

1442
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:51,933
- The giants don't
last that long.

1443
01:07:51,933 --> 01:07:54,067
They eat their own weight
every three or four days.

1444
01:07:54,067 --> 01:07:55,833
- But suppose they
find another way,

1445
01:07:55,833 --> 01:07:57,633
those passages down there.

1446
01:07:57,633 --> 01:07:59,533
- [Tom] They're crafty.

1447
01:07:59,533 --> 01:08:02,100
- [Joel] They did play
a cruise ship once

1448
01:08:02,100 --> 01:08:04,033
when I was a kid
but other than that.

1449
01:08:04,033 --> 01:08:05,467
Major.
Yes Doctor?

1450
01:08:05,467 --> 01:08:07,100
- Let's close it.

1451
01:08:07,100 --> 01:08:08,533
Ready?
- Aim.

1452
01:08:09,667 --> 01:08:11,067
- Let her go.

1453
01:08:11,067 --> 01:08:13,900
(explosion booms)

1454
01:08:15,767 --> 01:08:18,867
- I guess that does it.
- Wanna bet?

1455
01:08:23,733 --> 01:08:25,533
- [Joel] It seemed
like a good idea.

1456
01:08:25,533 --> 01:08:26,733
At first.
At first.

1457
01:08:32,900 --> 01:08:35,533
- [Crow] Hey your
apartment is great.

1458
01:08:40,533 --> 01:08:43,533
- This isn't the end of
anything, not for us.

1459
01:08:43,533 --> 01:08:45,167
It's the beginning.

1460
01:08:45,167 --> 01:08:48,400
- Hank all of us have
done our work now and

1461
01:08:48,400 --> 01:08:50,733
thank heaven it can be done
without any more tragedy.

1462
01:08:50,733 --> 01:08:53,500
And you still have your survey
of the volcanoes to make yet.

1463
01:08:53,500 --> 01:08:55,467
- [Joel] By the way you're
sitting on a hornets' nest.

1464
01:08:55,467 --> 01:08:57,367
- I'll be home every
night for dinner.

1465
01:08:58,567 --> 01:08:59,900
- I have to leave at once.

1466
01:08:59,900 --> 01:09:01,567
I should've left for the
States two months ago

1467
01:09:01,567 --> 01:09:02,767
to buy a cattle for the herd.

1468
01:09:02,767 --> 01:09:04,300
- [Tom] Did you leave
the water running?

1469
01:09:04,300 --> 01:09:07,067
- You'll be in Mexico
City for a week first huh?

1470
01:09:07,067 --> 01:09:08,633
- [Joel] Very powerful woman.

1471
01:09:08,633 --> 01:09:10,700
- I'll finish up my work with
Doc and I'll meet you there

1472
01:09:10,700 --> 01:09:12,400
and you can show me the town.

1473
01:09:12,400 --> 01:09:14,233
- [Crow] Well at the
city of 8 billion people.

1474
01:09:14,233 --> 01:09:15,567
You better go talk to
the chamber of commerce.

1475
01:09:15,567 --> 01:09:17,467
- A day, two days?

1476
01:09:17,467 --> 01:09:20,200
I don't want to settle
for just two days Hank.

1477
01:09:22,000 --> 01:09:23,800
- I don't want just
two days either.

1478
01:09:23,800 --> 01:09:25,167
- [Tom] I want five days.

1479
01:09:25,167 --> 01:09:28,300
Five nights, double
occupancy, air fare included!

1480
01:09:28,300 --> 01:09:30,467
- I don't want them
to fool me either.

1481
01:09:30,467 --> 01:09:31,800
- I'm not gonna.

1482
01:09:33,667 --> 01:09:35,633
I like you very much indeed
and I want you very much.

1483
01:09:39,833 --> 01:09:41,867
- [Tom] Your breath
is like mummy meat.

1484
01:09:45,167 --> 01:09:46,367
- [Crow] Cookie.

1485
01:09:46,367 --> 01:09:49,200
- [Joel] Meanwhile
at Hawaii 5 0.

1486
01:09:49,200 --> 01:09:50,733
- [Hank] Dr Scott!

1487
01:09:50,733 --> 01:09:52,167
Hello I can hardly hear you.

1488
01:09:52,167 --> 01:09:53,933
- This is Dr Vilasko.

1489
01:09:53,933 --> 01:09:55,767
- Oh Dr Vilasko,
how are you sir?

1490
01:09:55,767 --> 01:09:57,567
- [Crow] Well I'm tying
some details yeah.

1491
01:09:57,567 --> 01:09:59,867
Yeah it's perp's day
down here you know?

1492
01:10:01,067 --> 01:10:03,700
- Hank I regret to have
to complicate the plans

1493
01:10:03,700 --> 01:10:05,967
you and Dr Ramos
have made for so long

1494
01:10:05,967 --> 01:10:08,733
but some of my colleagues
here in Mexico are very

1495
01:10:08,733 --> 01:10:10,667
very anxious to talk
to you both at once.

1496
01:10:10,667 --> 01:10:14,400
- I don't really think
there's anything we can add

1497
01:10:14,400 --> 01:10:16,567
to what you already
know Dr Vilasko.

1498
01:10:16,567 --> 01:10:18,800
- I am with the Director
of Civilian Defense

1499
01:10:18,800 --> 01:10:21,100
and High Army Officers
right now Hank.

1500
01:10:21,100 --> 01:10:22,100
- [Tom] That's great.

1501
01:10:22,100 --> 01:10:23,633
- It is imperative that you both

1502
